{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-65720",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The period $T$ of the function is \n\n$$\n3\\pi -(-\\pi )=4\\pi .\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{sec}⁡(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{2\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get:\n\n$$\n4\\pi =\\frac{2\\pi }{B}\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{2\\pi }{4\\pi }=\\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the secant function. Since the local minimum of secant is $y=1$, we see that the function has been translated by $2$ units **up**. Hence, $D=2.$\n\nTherefore, $B+D=\\frac{1}{2}+2=\\frac{5}{2}.$\n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is:\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+2\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
